{"toolCallId":"call_d9a5359d26104ffa885fa15692585457","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"./AGENTS.md:251:| **Which level does this work need?**                                | `system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — deterministic scoring over LOC, file count and risk. |\n./README.md:423:- **`recommend-level.sh`** - analyze scope and risk to recommend the right documentation level\n./.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.0.md:82:- `spec/validate.sh`, `spec/create.sh`, `spec/repair-derived.cjs` and `spec/recommend-level.sh` for the packet lifecycle\n./.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/code-organization/directory-and-test-conventions.md:203:│   ├── recommend-level.sh\n./.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml:86:        command: \"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold {phase_threshold} --loc {estimated_loc} --files {estimated_files}\"\n./.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml:272:    note: \"recommend-level.sh scores LOC, file count and risk and decides the level; when its answer and judgment differ, go higher. decision-record.md and the other add-ons are lazy at every level, scaffolded on request\"\n./.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-implement.yaml:247:    note: \"recommend-level.sh scores LOC, file count and risk and decides the level; when its answer and judgment differ, go higher. decision-record.md and the other add-ons are lazy at every level, scaffolded on request\"\n./.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-complete.yaml:147:        command: \"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold {phase_threshold} --loc {estimated_loc} --files {estimated_files}\"\n./.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-complete.yaml:309:    note: \"recommend-level.sh scores LOC, file count and risk and decides the level; when its answer and judgment differ, go higher. decision-record.md and the other add-ons are lazy at every level, scaffolded on request\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:297:Run `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, which scores LOC, file count and risk; go higher when it disagrees with your judgment\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/level-decision-matrix.md:302:**LOC as one input to `recommend-level.sh`, which scores LOC, file count and risk together:**\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/addons/research.md.tmpl:490:<!-- FILL: Show one working example and its output. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500` prints one line. WEAK: Code below. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/addons/debug-delegation.md.tmpl:79:<!-- FILL: Give the specialist the files, the command and the evidence. GOOD: File `recommend-level.sh` line 510. Command `--quiet`. Output 3 lines. WEAK: See the code. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl:42:<!-- FILL: Fill the packet id, the level, the status and the date. GOOD: `004-recommend-level-quiet`. Level 1. Draft. 2026-10-24. WEAK: Packet TBD. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/plan.md.tmpl:67:<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/plan.md.tmpl:84:<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/plan.md.tmpl:102:<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl:86:<!-- FILL: Fill the folder name, the completion date and the level. Use the real date. GOOD: `004-recommend-level-quiet`. Completed 2026-10-24. Level 1. WEAK: Folder: TBD. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl:60:<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/tasks.md.tmpl:143:<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:74:<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/recommend-level-quiet`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:100:<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The recommend-level script prints a 17-line report, so a caller that needs only the level cannot parse the answer. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/core/spec.md.tmpl:171:<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:114:- `spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:514:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:621:| `recommend-level.sh` | analyze scope and risk to recommend the right level |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/template-authoring/level-1-packet-authored-from-card.md:74:BANNED OPERATIONS: git commit, git push, git checkout, git switch, git branch, git reset, git stash, generate-context.js, /speckit:save, and any edit outside specs/zz-pb-card/. Do not edit recommend-level.sh. Do not edit anything under .skilled/.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/template-authoring/level-1-packet-authored-from-card.md:79:3. Fill spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md and implementation-summary.md. Describe this feature in the packet and do not build it: a --quiet flag for .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh that prints only the final recommended-level line. Say in implementation-summary.md that the packet is planned and not implemented.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:44:2. Verify Step 1: Phase scoring runs (recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases)\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:61:$ bash \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\" --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold 0.6 --loc 500 --files 8\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:66:$ bash \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\" --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold 300 --loc 500 --files 8\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:22:- Real user request: `Please validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and tell me whether the expected signals are present: help output available for lifecycle entrypoints; upgrade regression suite passes; completene